<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercise xml:id="exercise-indexed-cartesian-products" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Indexed Cartesian products
  </title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Let <m> U_{ 1 } = \set{ 1 , 2 } </m>, <m> U_{ 2 } = \set{ 1 , 2 , 3 } </m>, and <m> U_{ 3 } = \set{ 0 , 1 } </m>, and consider the Cartesian product <m> U = \prod_{ k = 1 }^{ 3 }{ U_{ k } } </m>.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Write down the Cartesian product <m> U = \prod_{ k = 1 }^{ 3 }{ U_{ k } } </m> in roster notation.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        We have
        
        <md>
          <mrow>
            U \amp = \{ \of{ 1 , 1 , 0 } , \of{ 1 , 1 , 1 } , \of{ 1 , 2 , 0 } , \of{ 1 , 2 , 1 } , \of{ 1 , 3 , 0 } , \of{ 1 , 3 , 1 } ,
          </mrow>
          
          <mrow>
            \amp \qquad \of{ 2 , 1 , 0 } , \of{ 2 , 1 , 1 } , \of{ 2 , 2 , 0 } , \of{ 2 , 2 , 1 } , \of{ 2 , 3 , 0 } , \of{ 2 , 3 , 1 } \}
          </mrow>
        </md>.
      </p>
    </answer>
  </task>
  
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        For each index <m> k \in \set{ 1 , 2 , 3 } </m>, let <m> \pi_{ k } \colon U \to U_{ k } </m> be the projection map onto the <m> k </m>th factor. Compute <m> \pi_{ 1 } \of{ 2 , 3 , 0 } </m>, <m> \pi_{ 2 } \of{ 1 , 1 , 1 } </m>, and <m> \pi_{ 3 } \of{ 2 , 2 , 0 } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        We have
        
        <md>
          <mrow>
            \pi_{ 1 } \of{ 2 , 3 , 0 } \amp = 2 \amp \pi_{ 2 } \of{ 1 , 1 , 1 } \amp = 1 \amp \pi_{ 3 } \of{ 2 , 2 , 0 } \amp = 0
          </mrow>
        </md>.
      </p>
    </answer>
  </task>
</exercise>
